From 520732c4104142b24c14745a5b22eb972409d38c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 05:27:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): bare dashboard comments from a local agent
 process record an agent writer [daveey]

POST /api/plugins/kanban/tasks/<id>/comments recorded writer_kind='human' whenever the
client omitted writer_kind, so any dashboard-token holder (an agent's curl, a plugin) was
recorded as the operator. For a raw loopback TCP peer the endpoint now resolves the socket
owner (exact reversed tuple; per-process fallback for macOS) and walks its start-time
ancestry with the CLI's kanban_comment_writer: an agent marker or inconclusive walk -> agent.
Clean local ancestry and remote/unresolvable peers keep the legacy human default
(heuristic, not authentication). The raw peer is observed outside Uvicorn's unchanged
ProxyHeadersMiddleware so X-Forwarded-For cannot launder it. Linux/Darwin only; the
per-process socket scan runs only on Darwin (global inventory denied there).

The browser auto-opens of `hermes dashboard` (start_server, running-backend attach) and
`hermes webapp` now open the URL from a child interpreter with clean_launch_env(), and
`hermes desktop` launching an installed /Applications/Hermes.app passes clean_launch_env():
main() advertises HERMES_AGENT in os.environ for every command, so a browser or app started
with it would carry the agent markers and a person's drawer notes typed there would record
as an agent's. Windows opener children get CREATE_NO_WINDOW.

Verified: real token-holding marked curl -> agent (Linux test, unmocked); fresh isolated
Desktop drawer on a Mac -> human; Desktop SSH-target tunnels (Darwin and Linux sshd) ->
human; real BROWSER-script proof the opened browser has no agent markers; 24/24 mutations
killed.
